---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Cookies on ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: Clarity only after you accept`} description="Cookies on Statutory Pay: the calculators set none, and Microsoft Clarity analytics loads only after you accept in the banner. Each cookie, its lifetime and how to withdraw." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>This page completes the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>Nothing stored before you choose</h2><p>The redundancy, holiday, notice, maternity and sick pay calculators run in your browser and write no cookie. Until you accept analytics in the banner, nothing else is stored either; you can check it in your browser’s developer tools, under Storage.</p>
    <h2>Your choice itself</h2><p>Your answer to the banner sits in <code>localStorage</code> under <code>consent-choice</code>, purely so that you are not asked again on each page. It is not an identifier and does not leave your device, so PECR treats it as strictly necessary.</p>
    <h2>Microsoft Clarity, only once you accept</h2><p>Accepting loads Microsoft Clarity, operated by Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited. Clarity builds anonymous session recordings and heatmaps showing which pages are used, where visitors click and how far down they read. Dates, pay and the other details you enter are masked in the browser before anything is transmitted. It sets <code>_clck</code> for one year and <code>_clsk</code> for one day, and Microsoft may set <code>MUID</code> and <code>CLID</code> on its own domains. If you open a shared link that has your inputs in its address, that address is captured with the visit.</p>
    <h2>No advertising</h2><p>No adverts, no advertising cookie and no social media script are loaded.</p>
    <h2>Withdrawing</h2><p>“Cookie settings” in the footer brings the banner back; choose Decline and Clarity is no longer loaded. Clear the site data in your browser to delete cookies already placed.</p>
    <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
